---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Playground from '../../../components/Playground.astro';
import { url } from '../../../utils/paths';

const pageTitle = "Interactive Template & Cleaner Playground";
const pageDesc = "Test AutoTelegramForward's cleaner options, header/footer templates, and shortcodes in your browser with real-time output preview.";
---

<DocsLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDesc}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Tools', href: url('/tools/playground/') },
    { name: 'Playground', href: url('/tools/playground/') }
  ]}
  prev={{ title: 'All Features', href: url('/features/') }}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <p class="text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      This interactive sandbox runs entirely in your browser using pure client-side JavaScript. It simulates the exact transformation logic used in AutoTelegramForward's Python Core pipeline: URL and mention stripping, hashtag cleaning, phone number scrubbing, and shortcode interpolation.
    </p>

    <div class="not-prose my-6">
      <Playground />
    </div>

    <h2 id="how-it-works">How It Works in Production</h2>
    <p>
      In production, AutoTelegramForward executes this transformation pipeline inside <code>core/domain/services.py</code>:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Normalization:</strong> The raw Pyrogram message caption or text is normalized to standard Python strings, eliminating UTF-16 surrogates.</li>
      <li><strong>Cleaning:</strong> Cleaner options strip URLs, mentions, hashtags, emojis, or custom words according to your per-rule settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Shortcode Interpolation:</strong> Header and footer templates are populated with verified variables (<code>[[ORIGIN_NAME]]</code>, <code>[[ORIGIN_POST_ID]]</code>, <code>[[ORIGIN_POST_DATE]]</code>, etc.).</li>
      <li><strong>Dispatch:</strong> The assembled message is enqueued for delivery to destination chats via MTProto.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
